{
  "_about": "Order 264.8: which datasheet fact SETTLES that a standard's Part (a division whose own scope limits it to one construction) applies to this equipment. A family is named by the words a Part's scope uses for it (every word of one `scope_words` entry is in the Part's construction phrase) and is settled by a stated fact: the VALUE of a field (never its label) matches one of `patterns`, in one of the family's `roles`. Only the pressure-containing parts settle a construction (the shell, the heads, the design code): never a tube, trim, gasket, bolting, a seal or a lining. A negated hit (\"not welded\") settles nothing; a layer (cladding, lining) settles nothing; an `exclusive` family (the materials) is never settled when ANOTHER exclusive family is also stated on the shell or the heads, or when one value names two of them. A joint efficiency, a radiography or a PWHT note says nothing about the construction by itself and is not used. Only 'applies' is ever decided from here; a Part is never excluded from here. DRAFT: a client discipline engineer approves the lists before they are relied on. No standard and no Part is named.",
